    "directions": [
      "Combine all of the ingredients, except for the spareribs, in a bowl and whisk to combine. Set aside ½ cup of the sauce.",
      "Place the ribs in a non-reactive baking dish, pour the sauce on top, and turn to coat the ribs. Marinate in the refrigerator for 1 to 3 hours, turning the ribs once.",
      "Preheat the oven to 400°F and line a rimmed baking sheet with aluminum foil.",
      "Place the ribs on the prepared baking sheet and bake for 50 minutes, turning once halfway through the cooking time and basting with half of the reserved sauce.",
      "At the end of 50 minutes, remove the ribs from the oven and brush with the remaining sauce.",
      "Preheat the broiler. When hot, broil the ribs, meaty side up, until the ribs begin to char, about 5 minutes.",
      "Remove from the broiler, hack the ribs apart with a cleaver or chef’s knife, and serve."
    ],
